<script>
import Doc from '#src/lib/Doc.abide'
import Example from '#src/lib/Example.abide'
import Section from '#src/lib/Section.abide'

import AnchorWidth from './lib/AnchorWidth.abide'
import anchorWidth from './lib/AnchorWidth.abide' with { type: 'text' }
import ArrowInset from './lib/ArrowInset.abide'
import arrowInset from './lib/ArrowInset.abide' with { type: 'text' }
import FilterPanel from './lib/FilterPanel.abide'
import filterPanel from './lib/FilterPanel.abide' with { type: 'text' }
import LitTrigger from './lib/LitTrigger.abide'
import litTrigger from './lib/LitTrigger.abide' with { type: 'text' }
</script>

<Doc
    seeAlso={['/behaviors/dismissible', '/headless/menu', '/headless/combobox']}
    tests={[
        {
            path: 'packages/dogfood/examples/crm/src/pipeline/lib/StageFilter.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('the stage button opens its panel as a popover under it, and a pick shuts it'",
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/dogfood/examples/crm/src/pipeline/lib/StageFilter.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('Escape, a press outside and a second press on the button each shut the stage panel'",
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/overlays.test.ts',
            from: ["test('a side with no room flips to the opposite one"],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/overlays.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('the arrow keeps arrowInset from the corners, and an edge too short for both centers it",
            ],
        },
    ]}
>
    <Section level={3} title="Open a filter panel under its button">
        <p>Spread <code>trigger</code> on the button and <code>popover</code> on the panel. The
            button opens and closes it, and a press outside or Escape closes it. It sits in the
            top layer, placed on the side it is given and flipped where there is no room, and
            <code>data-side</code> says which it took.</p>
        <Example code={filterPanel}><FilterPanel /></Example>
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Make a list as wide as the field it suggests for">
        <p>Spread <code>anchor</code> on a field that opens the popover some other way, here
            by typing, and write <code>open</code> from what opens it. <code>--anchor-width</code> is the
            anchor's width, kept current as it resizes.</p>
        <Example code={anchorWidth}><AnchorWidth /></Example>
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Point an arrow at the button, clear of the rounded corners">
        <p>The popover writes <code>--arrow-offset</code>: how far along its facing edge the
            button's middle falls, kept <code>arrowInset</code> pixels from each end so an arrow
            drawn there clears the corners.</p>
        <Example code={arrowInset}><ArrowInset /></Example>
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Keep the button lit while its panel is open">
        <p>The trigger carries <code>aria-expanded="true"</code> while the popover shows, and the
            popover carries <code>data-open</code>.</p>
        <Example code={litTrigger}><LitTrigger /></Example>
    </Section>
</Doc>
